## Working Preferences

### Token Efficiency
- Use bash for bulk operations (cat, grep) instead of reading files one at a time
- Don't create new .md files — edit existing ones
- Batch multi-file changes: plan → read all → apply all → verify once

### File Safety
- Archive old files to `archive/` — never delete without asking
- Use `-..delete` suffix for uncertain removals (e.g., `old-component-..delete.tsx`)
- Ask user approval before: deleting files, force pushing, dropping tables, overwriting configs

### Working Scope
- Stay within this project folder unless explicitly told otherwise
- Ask before accessing any file outside this project
- Previous approval to leave scope doesn't carry to new sessions

### Communication
- State what you're about to do before doing it for large changes
- Ask for approval on architectural decisions before implementing
- When corrected, update `memory/MEMORY.md` Locked Preferences immediately

